{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.HadronQSelfCorrection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.HadronQSelfCorrection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hadron_q_self_correction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hadron_q_self_correction","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hadron-q-self-correction.lean#L138-L144","doc":"Top-level alias matching the manifest declaration: the\nself-deformation is the net signed crossing count over `A²`,\nweighted by `ℏ_q² = (1 - q₀⁻¹)²`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:hadron-q-self-correction","label":"prop:hadron-q-self-correction","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hadron-q-self-correction.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.qEff_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.qEff_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hadron-q-self-correction.lean#L128-L136","doc":"q_eff > 1 when q₀ > 1: the effective parameter stays in the\nnon-classical regime (self-deformation is too small to change this). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.differentialShift_small","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.differentialShift_small","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hadron-q-self-correction.lean#L108-L126","doc":"The differential shift is small: for all A and q₀ = 1.1097,\nΔq_eff < ℏ_q² < 0.01. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.differentialShift_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.differentialShift_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hadron-q-self-correction.lean#L96-L106","doc":"The differential shift is non-negative when A ≥ 1 and q₀ > 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.differentialShift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.differentialShift","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hadron-q-self-correction.lean#L89-L94","doc":"The differential shift equals (A-1)/A² · ℏ_q² and is always\npositive: the daughter nucleus (one more proton) has a higher\neffective q than the parent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.deltaDeltaQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.deltaDeltaQ","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hadron-q-self-correction.lean#L79-L87","doc":"Differential self-deformation across a single beta decay:\nΔq_eff = δq(p+1, n-1) - δq(p, n).\n\nThis is the physically relevant quantity for half-lives:\nit determines how the effective Q-value differs from the\nbackground-q prediction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.deltaQ_neg_neutron_rich","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.deltaQ_neg_neutron_rich","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hadron-q-self-correction.lean#L65-L77","doc":"For neutron-rich nuclei (n > p), the self-deformation is negative:\nthe excess of negative crossings slightly reduces q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.netSignedCrossing_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.netSignedCrossing_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hadron-q-self-correction.lean#L54-L63","doc":"The net signed crossing count is non-positive for neutron-rich\nnuclei (`p < n`): the triangular number `C(n,2)` dominates `C(p,2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.qEff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.qEff","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hadron-q-self-correction.lean#L49-L52","doc":"Effective substrate parameter: q_eff = q₀ + δq. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.deltaQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.deltaQ","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hadron-q-self-correction.lean#L41-L47","doc":"Self-deformation of the substrate parameter by a nucleus.\nδq(p,n) = ℓ_net(p,n)/A² · ℏ_q² where ℏ_q = 1 - q₀⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.netSignedCrossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.netSignedCrossing","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hadron-q-self-correction.lean#L36-L39","doc":"Net signed crossing number: ℓ_net(p,n) = C(p,2) - C(n,2). ","signatureChunk":0}]}